<description>
Complete scaled copies of the blue source template at matching red marker squares.

Input structure
- A black background contains one 4-connected mixed-color template object and detached same-color target squares.
- The template has source-color pixels and marker-color pixels; the detached marker objects are solid k x k squares.
- The output shape is unchanged.

Rule
- Use the template bbox as the pattern coordinate system.
- Group target marker squares into sets whose top-left corners match the template marker coordinates at one common scale k.
- For each matched group, scale every source-color template cell to a k x k block and paint it at that instance's origin, clipping any part outside the grid.

Key insight
The detached marker squares are enlarged copies of the template's marker cells; their side length gives the scale for copying the source-color cells.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "source-color cells in the mixed template object s with marker-color control cells",
  "dst": "detached marker-color square groups d",
  "match_cond": "d squares have one common side length k and their top-left corners match s marker-cell offsets scaled by k",
  "transform": "paint each s source cell as a k x k block at the matched instance origin, clipping off-grid and preserving existing marker cells"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 14-20 rows x 12-21 cols, black background
  colors: source=1(blue), marker=2(red) [observed]
  template:
    description: one 4-connected mixed-color object containing source-color and marker-color cells
    bbox: 1-4 rows x 3-4 cols, area 4-8 cells [observed]
    source_cells: 3-6 forming an arbitrary connected shape
    marker_cells: 1-2, 4-connected to source cells so whole template is one 4-connected component
    no_overlap: source and marker cells occupy distinct positions within bbox; bbox may have holes
  target_squares:
    count: 1-4 solid k x k squares of marker color, detached from template
    scale_k: 1-3 per square; within one instance group all squares share the same k
    instances: 1-3 groups; each group has exactly #marker_cells squares whose top-left offsets match template marker-cell offsets scaled by k
    all_targets_assigned: every target square belongs to exactly one instance group
  layout:
    template and all target squares are non-overlapping, separated by >=2 cells of background
    scaled source blocks painted in output must not overlap each other or existing marker squares
    clipping allowed -- painted blocks may extend to grid edge and be clipped [observed]
  output:
    same grid size; for each instance, paint each template source cell as a k x k block of source color at (origin + rel * k); template and markers preserved

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size and 2 colors (source, marker).
    2. Design a small template pattern with S source cells and M marker cells (M=1-2) that is 4-connected.
    3. Choose 1-3 instance groups, each with a scale k in 1-3. For each group, compute the full scaled pattern (source blocks + marker squares) footprint.
    4. Place all instance footprints on the grid ensuring no overlap with each other. Place the template ensuring no overlap with instances.
    5. Build output grid with template + all marker squares + all painted source blocks.
    6. Build input grid by removing the painted source blocks from the output (keep template and marker squares only).
    7. Validate: template is the only mixed-color 4-connected component; each target square is a solid k x k marker-color block; all source blocks fit or clip within grid.
